          "en": "Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: He entered the house of a woman from the tribe of Ahmas named Zaynab and found her silent. He asked, « Why is she not speaking? » They said, « She performed Hajj in silence. » He said to her, « Speak, for this is not permissible. This is a practice from the Days of Ignorance. » She spoke and asked, « Who are you? » He said, « A man from the Muhajirun. » She asked, « Which of the Muhajirun? » He said, « From Quraysh. » She asked, « From which part of Quraysh? » He said, « You are indeed inquisitive! I am Abu Bakr. » She asked, « How long will this good matter that Allah has brought after the Days of Ignorance last? » He said, « It will last as long as your leaders guide you rightly. » She asked, « Who are the leaders? » He said, « Did your people not have heads and nobles whom they obeyed? » She said, « Yes. » He said, « They are the leaders for the people. »",
